ven-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fortman</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name><name><surname>McPhillips</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Roblin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Yood</surname><given-names>MU</given-names></name><name><surname>Platt</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>H Gurwitz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of prescription medications with a potential for fetal harm among pregnant women</article-title><source>Pharmacoepidemiol Drug Saf</source><year>2006</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>546</fpage><lpage>554</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16586470</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/pds.1235</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eadie</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antiepileptic drugs as human teratogens</article-title><source>Expert Opin Drug Saf</source><year>2008</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>195</fpage><lpage>209</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18324882</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1517/14740338.7.2.195</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>